{"id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:hodge-star-euclidean-single","title":"prop:hodge-star-euclidean-single","path":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.md","line":4269,"body":"","kind":"theorem","status":"not_started","tex":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex#prop:hodge-star-euclidean-single","uses":["[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:hodge-star-graded]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:hodge-star-pointwise]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:wedge-covectors-sign]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:wedge-covectors-repeat-zero]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:inner-k-covectors]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:wedge-covectors]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex","label":"prop:hodge-star-euclidean-single","line":7205,"source":"\\begin{proposition}[The Hodge Star of a Coordinate Covector]\n\\label{prop:hodge-star-euclidean-single}\n\n\\uses{prop:hodge-star-graded, prop:hodge-star-pointwise, lem:wedge-covectors-sign, lem:wedge-covectors-repeat-zero, def:inner-k-covectors, def:wedge-covectors}\n\n\n\n\\dcref{ch2:2-19}\n\nFor an oriented orthonormal coframe $(e^0,\\ldots,e^{n-1})$,\n\\[\n{*} e^i=(-1)^i e^{i_1}\\wedge\\cdots\\wedge e^{i_{n-1}},\n\\]\nwhere the remaining indices are increasing; in $1$-based indexing the sign is $(-1)^{i-1}$.\n\\end{proposition}\n\\begin{proof}\n\n\\uses{prop:hodge-star-graded,prop:hodge-star-pointwise,lem:wedge-covectors-sign,lem:wedge-covectors-repeat-zero,def:inner-k-covectors,def:wedge-covectors}\n\\sketch Verify the star characterization on coframe covectors. The cyclic reordering contributes $(-1)^i$ when the index agrees; otherwise the wedge repeats a covector and vanishes.\n\\end{proof}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Proposition</div></section>[The Hodge Star of a Coordinate Covector] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-70726f703a686f6467652d737461722d6575636c696465616e2d73696e676c65\"></span> <p></p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23prop%3Ahodge-star-graded\">↗ prop:hodge-star-graded</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23prop%3Ahodge-star-pointwise\">↗ prop:hodge-star-pointwise</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Awedge-covectors-sign\">↗ lem:wedge-covectors-sign</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Awedge-covectors-repeat-zero\">↗ lem:wedge-covectors-repeat-zero</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23def%3Ainner-k-covectors\">↗ def:inner-k-covectors</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23def%3Awedge-covectors\">↗ def:wedge-covectors</a> <p></p><span class=\"tex-source-references\" role=\"list\" style=\"display:block\"><span class=\"tex-dcref\" role=\"listitem\" style=\"display:block\">1. ch2:2-19</span></span><p></p>For an oriented orthonormal coframe <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$(e^0,\\ldots ,e^{n-1})$\">$(e^0,\\ldots ,e^{n-1})$</span>, <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"true\" data-tex=\"\\[  {*} e^i=(-1)^i e^{i_1}\\wedge \\cdots \\wedge e^{i_{n-1}},  \\]\">\\[  {*} e^i=(-1)^i e^{i_1}\\wedge \\cdots \\wedge e^{i_{n-1}},  \\]</span> where the remaining indices are increasing; in <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$1$\">$1$</span>-based indexing the sign is <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$(-1)^{i-1}$\">$(-1)^{i-1}$</span>.  <section class=\"theorem proof\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Proof</div><p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23prop%3Ahodge-star-graded\">↗ prop:hodge-star-graded</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23prop%3Ahodge-star-pointwise\">↗ prop:hodge-star-pointwise</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Awedge-covectors-sign\">↗ lem:wedge-covectors-sign</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Awedge-covectors-repeat-zero\">↗ lem:wedge-covectors-repeat-zero</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23def%3Ainner-k-covectors\">↗ def:inner-k-covectors</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23def%3Awedge-covectors\">↗ def:wedge-covectors</a> \\sketch Verify the star characterization on coframe covectors. The cyclic reordering contributes <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$(-1)^i$\">$(-1)^i$</span> when the index agrees; otherwise the wedge repeats a covector and vanishes. </p><span class=\"qed\" aria-label=\"证毕\" style=\"display:block;text-align:right\">□</span></section>","warnings":["部分 TeX 排版细节未完整还原（已保留可读内容）: sketch"]},"previous":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:wedge-covectors-repeat-zero","next":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:wedge-covectors-sign","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:hodge-star-graded","title":"prop:hodge-star-graded","label":"prop:hodge-star-graded"},